WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:06.386
After lunch the earl summoned Cedric to the library.

2
00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:11.656
"Thank you for the toys!" Cedric cried as he raced into the room.

3
00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:16.713
"There's one that's like baseball, only you play it on a board with pegs.

4
00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:21.639
I tried to explain it to Mrs. Mellon, but she didn't understand the game.

5
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.125
You know all about baseball, right?"

6
00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:33.461
"I'm afraid I don't," the earl said. "It's an American sport."

7
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:41.858
"Would you like me to show you my game? Or does your foot hurt too much right now?"

8
00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:45.359
"Go and get the game," the earl said.

9
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.721
Once again the earl noticed Cedric's thoughtfulness.

10
00:00:50.722 --> 00:00:54.267
He almost smiled when Cedric returned.

11
00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:59.212
"May I pull that table over to your chair?" Cedric asked.

12
00:00:59.213 --> 00:01:04.706
"Ring for the footman, and he'll move it for you," the earl said.

13
00:01:04.707 --> 00:01:09.079
"I can do it myself. It's not too heavy."

14
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:14.428
The earl watched with amusement as Cedric dragged the table into place.

15
00:01:14.429 --> 00:01:18.632
Then he took the game from the box and arranged it on the table.

16
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:22.714
Cedric explained how each peg represented a player.

17
00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:27.746
Finally he summarized the rules of baseball for the earl.

18
00:01:27.747 --> 00:01:36.548
"And that's how you score a run," Cedric said. "Let's play!"

19
00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:42.923
Cedric and his grandfather were absorbed in the game when a footman announced a visitor.

20
00:01:42.924 --> 00:01:48.440
Reverend Mordaunt, minister of the village church, had arrived full of dread.

21
00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:53.333
He'd heard that the earl's gout was bad and that Cedric had arrived.

22
00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:58.120
He was sure the earl would be in a worse mood than usual.

23
00:01:58.121 --> 00:02:02.681
So he was surprised to find the earl having fun with Cedric.

24
00:02:02.682 --> 00:02:07.148
"They seem to be getting along," Reverend Mordaunt thought.

25
00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:12.060
"But I'm sure his mood will change when he learns why I'm here.

26
00:02:12.061 --> 00:02:18.231
He always thinks his tenants are to blame when they need help."

27
00:02:18.232 --> 00:02:26.607
"Be careful," Cedric said to his grandfather. "One more out, and I win."

28
00:02:26.608 --> 00:02:35.503
"The game's not over yet." The earl realized the minister was waiting to be greeted.

29
00:02:35.504 --> 00:02:38.850
"Good afternoon, Reverend Mordaunt.

30
00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:43.820
As you can see, I'm trying something different."

31
00:02:43.821 --> 00:02:47.106
The earl laid his hand on Cedric's shoulder.

32
00:02:47.107 --> 00:02:52.109
"This is the new Lord Fauntleroy.

33
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:58.793
Cedric, this is Reverend Mordaunt."

34
00:02:58.794 --> 00:03:03.619
Cedric shook hands with the minister and then leaned against his grandfather's chair.

35
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.464
"Take a seat, reverend."

36
00:03:07.465 --> 00:03:12.046
The usual stern look had returned to the earl's face.

37
00:03:12.047 --> 00:03:16.459
"Why are you here? Who's in trouble now?"

38
00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:22.384
"One of your tenant farmers has been sick for a long time," the minister began.

39
00:03:22.385 --> 00:03:27.002
"Now he's behind on the rent and about to be evicted.

40
00:03:27.003 --> 00:03:34.891
His wife begged me to talk to you. If they have to leave, they'll starve. He's a good man—"

41
00:03:34.892 --> 00:03:42.153
"That sounds just like Mary and her husband!" Cedric looked eagerly at his grandfather.

42
00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:45.593
"Remember how I used your money to help them?"

43
00:03:45.594 --> 00:03:50.993
"So what would you do in this case?" the earl asked.

44
00:03:50.994 --> 00:03:57.453
"I'd give them time to catch up on the rent and send them some food."

45
00:03:57.454 --> 00:04:01.744
"You heard his lordship," the earl said to the minister.

46
00:04:01.745 --> 00:04:04.581
"Tell my tenant the good news.

47
00:04:04.582 --> 00:04:11.399
And on your way out, tell my cook to send them a basket of food every day."

48
00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.745
After Reverend Mordaunt left, Cedric asked to visit his mother.

49
00:04:16.746 --> 00:04:20.380
The earl wanted to cut that tie as soon as possible.

50
00:04:20.381 --> 00:04:27.762
"You can go another day. There's something for you to see in the stables now."

51
00:04:27.763 --> 00:04:31.909
"I'm sorry, but my mother is expecting me."

52
00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:36.044
"Don't you want to see your pony?"

53
00:04:36.045 --> 00:04:45.874
Cedric looked shocked. "My pony? Mine—like all the things upstairs?"

54
00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:50.705
The earl knew his grandson couldn't resist this temptation.

55
00:04:50.706 --> 00:04:55.101
"You can visit your mother tomorrow."

56
00:04:55.102 --> 00:04:59.090
"No, I can't," Cedric said firmly.

57
00:04:59.091 --> 00:05:03.708
"I've been missing Mama all morning, so I know she's missing me."

58
00:05:03.709 --> 00:05:15.701
The earl heaved an exasperated sigh. "Fine, you may visit your mother."

59
00:05:15.702 --> 00:05:21.574
Half an hour later, the two of them settled into the carriage.

60
00:05:21.575 --> 00:05:29.117
"I think you must be the best person in the world." Cedric turned toward his grandfather.

61
00:05:29.118 --> 00:05:33.145
"Me?" the earl said in surprise.

62
00:05:33.146 --> 00:05:36.720
"You help so many people.

63
00:05:36.721 --> 00:05:43.145
Mr. Hobbs thought earls were tyrants, but you're the kindest man I know.

64
00:05:43.146 --> 00:05:47.768
When I grow up, I want to be just like you."

65
00:05:47.769 --> 00:05:55.165
"Just like me." The earl turned away so he didn't have to face Cedric.

66
00:05:55.166 --> 00:06:00.899
He was deep in thought when they arrived at the cottage.

67
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.473
"I'll help you out," Cedric said as the carriage door opened.

68
00:06:05.474 --> 00:06:10.705
The earl shook his head. "I'm not getting out."

69
00:06:10.706 --> 00:06:18.238
"Not getting out?" Cedric said. "My mother will be disappointed."

70
00:06:18.239 --> 00:06:22.981
"I'm not so sure about that," the earl muttered.

71
00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:27.899
"Tell her not even a new pony could keep you away."

72
00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:37.887
The earl watched Cedric run up the drive and into his mother's arms.

